  {
    "id": "eli",
    "name": "Eli",
    "sex": "male",
    "era": "Judges",
    "summary": "The priest at Shiloh who watches Hannah pray and later trains the child Samuel. First Samuel calls his sons Hophni and Phinehas “sons of Belial”, a harsh description of their wrongdoing. They misuse their office. Eli rebukes them but does not stop them. An unnamed man of God warns of judgment on Eli's family. The account later describes the Lord giving Samuel a similar warning. At ninety-eight, Eli hears that the ark is taken and his sons are dead. He falls from his seat and dies. The text says he judged Israel forty years.",
