  {
    "id": "samuel",
    "name": "Samuel",
    "sex": "male",
    "era": "Judges",
    "summary": "Elkanah and Hannah's son, given to serve the Lord at Shiloh under Eli. First Samuel describes the Lord calling him as a child. The text presents him as a prophet known from Dan to Beersheba. He judges Israel on a yearly circuit and lives at Ramah. He anoints Saul as leader and later anoints David among his brothers. He rebukes Saul, saying obedience is better than sacrifice. The book covers the end of the judges and the start of the kingdom. It says Samuel judged Israel throughout his life.",
