    "id": "david",
    "name": "David",
    "sex": "male",
    "era": "Monarchy",
    "summary": "Jesse's youngest son from Bethlehem, summoned from the sheep and then anointed by Samuel. He kills Goliath with a sling and stone and serves Saul. He later flees Saul, leading an outlaw group in the wilderness and at Ziklag. After Saul's death, he becomes king at Hebron. The account gives him seven and a half years there and thirty-three in Jerusalem. It describes the Lord promising him a lasting royal line and throne. Nathan confronts him over Bathsheba and Uriah's death. The book also describes Absalom's revolt. The New Testament names David in Jesus' family list and Paul's speech at Antioch.",
